# Simple c++ file explorer

This is a very simple file explorer made as my first ever c++ project.
the project allows you to do a load of commands listed below in a terminal to interact with your files and to clean them up. For me the combine command is especially useful as I can move all of my downloaded pictures into one folder instantly.

<b>Do be careful to not delete any important files</b>

## all commands:
1) 'help': Shows a list of commands
2) "'dir': shows the current directory"
3) "'newdir <dirName>': creates a new directory in the curret one"
4) "'cdir <dirName>': change the directory to one that the current directory contains"
5) "'updir': go up one directory if possible"
6) << "'new <fileName>': creates a new file"
7) << "'rename <fileName, newFileName>': renames the chosen file or directory to the new name"
8) << "'del <delPath>': deletes the chosen file or directory"
9) << "'delempt': deletes all the files from the current directory which are empty"
10) << "'combine <fileExtention>': combines all the files with the given extention into a folder"
11) << "'edit <fileName>': go in to editing mode for a txt file"
12) << "'exit': ends the program";

## How to build the project yourself:
1) download `main.cpp`
2) You will need to have c++ compiler, I use g++
3) In the console search to the downloaded files folder
4) run the command ```g++ main.cpp -o main``` to compile the project
5) run the .exe file ```./main```

